                            <comment id="15179483" author="githubbot" created="Fri, 4 Mar 2016 07:07:26 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;GitHub user zhongneu opened a pull request:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/760&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/760&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-716&quot; title=&quot;Deadlock in RemoteInterpreter.open &amp;amp; RemoteInterpreter.init&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-716&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-716&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; protect the whole spark repl init process&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;
		&lt;ol&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;What is this PR for?&lt;br/&gt;
    ZeppelinContext may not be initialized properly in concurrent mode:&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;/ol&gt;
		&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;    When I create &amp;amp; run multiple notebooks using rest API concurrently, I can see such errors if the jobs trying to use ZeppelinContext:&lt;br/&gt;
    ```&lt;br/&gt;
    &amp;lt;console&amp;gt;:23: error: not found: value z&lt;br/&gt;
    ```&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    I think this issue can be reproduced by:&lt;br/&gt;
    1. create 4 - 5 new notebooks with content: `println(z)`&lt;br/&gt;
    2. use rest API to run the newly created notebooks concurrently&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    It seems the issue is gone after I expand the lock to protect the whole process of spark REPL initializing / binding. &lt;/p&gt;

